terraform apply
Step 1 - Create a New Relic API Key

Terraform uses a User API Key (NRAK-xxxx).

Go to

API Keys

Administration → API Keys

Create

User Key

Prefix:

NRAK-

You will also need

Account ID
Region
US
EU

The New Relic provider requires your account ID, API key, and region to authenticate.

Step 2 - Install Terraform
terraform version
Step 3 - Create Provider
terraform {
  required_providers {
    newrelic = {
      source  = "newrelic/newrelic"
      version = "~> 3.0"
    }
  }
}

provider "newrelic" {
  account_id = var.account_id
  api_key    = var.api_key
  region     = "US"
}

Store secrets in variables or environment variables instead of hardcoding them. The provider supports this configuration approach.

variables.tf
variable "account_id" {}

variable "api_key" {
  sensitive = true
}
terraform.tfvars
account_id = "12345678"
api_key    = "NRAK-xxxxxxxxxxxx"
Step 4 - Resources

For Alerts

resource "newrelic_alert_policy" "prod" {

}

For NRQL Alert

resource "newrelic_nrql_alert_condition" "cpu" {

}

For Synthetic Monitor

resource "newrelic_synthetics_monitor" "homepage" {

}

New Relic recommends using newrelic_nrql_alert_condition for alert conditions instead of the older newrelic_alert_condition, which is deprecated.

Step 5 - Import Existing Resources
Import Alert Policy

Example

terraform import \
newrelic_alert_policy.prod \
123456:987654

Format

policy_id:account_id

This composite ID format is required by the provider.

Import NRQL Alert

Example

terraform import \
newrelic_nrql_alert_condition.cpu \
123456:987654
Import Synthetic Monitor

Example

terraform import \
newrelic_synthetics_monitor.homepage \
abcd1234-5678

Import support is available for Synthetics monitor resources.

Step 6 - Generate Terraform Code

Terraform import only imports the state.

It does not generate

main.tf

You'll need to:

terraform state show RESOURCE

Example

terraform state show newrelic_alert_policy.prod

Output

resource "newrelic_alert_policy" "prod" {
  incident_preference = "PER_POLICY"
  name = "Production Policy"
}

Copy this output into

alerts.tf

Repeat for every resource.

Step 7 - Organize Repository

A typical layout:

terraform-newrelic/

│
├── provider.tf
├── variables.tf
├── terraform.tfvars
├── alerts.tf
├── synthetics.tf
├── outputs.tf
├── versions.tf
│
└── .github/
      workflows/
