Step 8 - Push into GitHub
git init

git add .

git commit -m "Initial New Relic Terraform"

git remote add origin https://github.com/Org/newrelic-iac.git

git push -u origin main
Step 9 - GitHub Actions

Example workflow

name: Terraform

on:
  push:
    branches:
      - main

jobs:

  terraform:

    runs-on: ubuntu-latest

    steps:

    - uses: actions/checkout@v4

    - uses: hashicorp/setup-terraform@v3

    - run: terraform init

    - run: terraform validate

    - run: terraform plan
      env:
        TF_VAR_account_id: ${{ secrets.NR_ACCOUNT_ID }}
        TF_VAR_api_key: ${{ secrets.NR_API_KEY }}

Store NR_ACCOUNT_ID and NR_API_KEY as GitHub repository secrets.

Useful New Relic Terraform Resources
Resource	Purpose
newrelic_alert_policy	Alert policies
newrelic_nrql_alert_condition	NRQL alert conditions
newrelic_notification_destination	Notification destinations
newrelic_notification_channel	Notification channels
newrelic_workflow	Incident workflows
newrelic_synthetics_monitor	Synthetic monitors
newrelic_one_dashboard	Dashboards
APIs Used

The Terraform provider interacts with New Relic's APIs behind the scenes, primarily through:

NerdGraph (GraphQL API) for modern resource management.
Legacy REST APIs for a few older resources where applicable.

You do not need to call these APIs directly when using Terraform—the provider handles API interactions for you.

