Recommended for your use case

Since you mentioned you want to import all existing New Relic alerts and monitors into GitHub, I recommend an automated migration workflow:

Export all Alert Policies, NRQL Conditions, Synthetics Monitors, Notification Channels, and Workflows from your New Relic account.
Import them into Terraform state.
Generate .tf files organized by resource type.
Store the code in a GitHub repository.
Configure a GitHub Actions pipeline to run terraform fmt, validate, plan, and apply.
Use a remote backend (such as Azure Storage or Terraform Cloud) to manage the Terraform state safely.

Given your experience with GitHub Actions and Azure DevOps migrations, this approach will make your New Relic configuration fully version-controlled and integrated into your CI/CD process.
